      * R, a *note ring: (Macaulay2Doc)Ring,, defined as a *note gaussianRing:
        (GraphicalModels)gaussianRing, of *note Graph: (Graphs)Graph,, or *note
        Digraph: (Graphs)Digraph,, or *note Bigraph: (StatGraphs)Bigraph,, or
        *note MixedGraph: (StatGraphs)MixedGraph,
  * Outputs:
      * an *note integer: (Macaulay2Doc)ZZ,, the ML-degree of the model

Description
===========

This function computes the ML-degree of a graphical model. It takes as input a
*note gaussianRing: (GraphicalModels)gaussianRing, of a *note Graph:
(Graphs)Graph,, or a *note Digraph: (Graphs)Digraph,, or a *note Bigraph:
(StatGraphs)Bigraph,, or a  *note MixedGraph: (StatGraphs)MixedGraph,. It
computes the degree of the score equation ideal given by *note scoreEquations:
scoreEquations, with a random sample data matrix.

We compute the ML-degree of the 4-cycle:

+-------------------------------------+
|i1 : G=graph{{1,2},{2,3},{3,4},{4,1}}|
|                                     |
|o1 = Graph{1 => {2, 4}}              |
|           2 => {1, 3}               |
|           3 => {2, 4}               |
|           4 => {1, 3}               |
|                                     |
|o1 : Graph                           |
+-------------------------------------+
|i2 : MLdegree(gaussianRing G)        |
|                                     |
|o2 = 5                               |
+-------------------------------------+

