scoreEquations -- score equations of the log-likelihood function of a Gaussian graphical model
**********************************************************************************************

  * Usage: 
        scoreEquations(R,U)
  * Inputs:
      * R, a *note ring: (Macaulay2Doc)Ring,, defined as a *note gaussianRing:
        (GraphicalModels)gaussianRing, of *note Graph: (Graphs)Graph,, or *note
        Digraph: (Graphs)Digraph,, or *note Bigraph: (StatGraphs)Bigraph,, or
        *note MixedGraph: (StatGraphs)MixedGraph,
      * U, a *note matrix: (Macaulay2Doc)Matrix,, or *note List:
        (Macaulay2Doc)List, of sample data. Alternatively, the input can be the
        sample covariance *note Matrix: (Macaulay2Doc)Matrix, by setting the
        optional input *note SampleData: SampleData, to false
  * *note Optional inputs: (Macaulay2Doc)using functions with optional inputs,:
      * *note CovarianceMatrix:
        scoreEquations_lp_pd_pd_pd_cmCovarianceMatrix=>_pd_pd_pd_rp, => ...,
        default value false, output covariance matrix
      * *note RealPrecision: scoreEquations_lp_pd_pd_pd_cmRealPrecision=>_pd_pd
        _pd_rp, => ..., default value 53, the number of bits of precision to
        use in the computation
      * *note SampleData: scoreEquations_lp_pd_pd_pd_cmSampleData=>_pd_pd_pd_rp
        , => ..., default value true, input sample covariance matrix instead of
        sample data
      * *note Saturate: scoreEquations_lp_pd_pd_pd_cmSaturate=>_pd_pd_pd_rp, =>
        ..., default value true, whether to saturate
      * *note SaturateOptions:
        scoreEquations_lp_pd_pd_pd_cmSaturateOptions=>_pd_pd_pd_rp, => ...,
        default value new OptionTable from {Strategy => null, BasisElementLimit
        => infinity, DegreeLimit => {}, MinimalGenerators => true, PairLimit =>
        infinity}, use options from "saturate"
  * Outputs:
      * a *note sequence: (Macaulay2Doc)Sequence,, consisting either of (Ideal)
        or (Ideal,Matrix) where the ideal is generated by the score equations
        of the log-likelihood function of the Gaussian model and the matrix is
        the symbolic covariance matrix of the model

Description
===========

This function computes the score equations that arise from taking partial
derivatives of the log-likelihood function of the concentration matrix (the
inverse of the covariance matrix) of a Gaussian graphical statistical model and
returns the ideal generated by such equations.

The input of this function is a *note gaussianRing:
(GraphicalModels)gaussianRing, and statistical data. The latter can be given as
a matrix or a list of observations. The rows of the matrix or the elements of
the list are observation vectors given as lists. It is possible to input the
sample covariance matrix directly by using the optional input *note SampleData:
SampleData,.

+-----------------------------------------------------------------------------+
|i1 : G = mixedGraph(digraph {{1,2},{1,3},{2,3},{3,4}},bigraph{{3,4}});       |
+-----------------------------------------------------------------------------+
|i2 : R = gaussianRing(G);                                                    |
