solverMLE(...,Saturate=>...) -- whether to saturate
***************************************************

  * Usage: 
        solverMLE(G,U,Saturate=>b)
  * Inputs:
      * b, a *note Boolean value: (Macaulay2Doc)Boolean,, default is true

Description
===========



*note solverMLE(...,Saturate=>...):
solverMLE_lp_pd_pd_pd_cmSaturate=>_pd_pd_pd_rp, is set to true by default. If
we set *note Saturate: Saturate, to false in *note solverMLE: solverMLE,,
saturation will not be performed when computing the score equations of the
log-likelihood function, see *note scoreEquations(...,Saturate=>...):
scoreEquations_lp_pd_pd_pd_cmSaturate=>_pd_pd_pd_rp,.

If the ideal returned by *note scoreEquations: scoreEquations, has positive
dimension, *note solverMLE: solverMLE, gives this ideal as output.

On the other hand, if we obtain a zero-dimensional ideal in *note
scoreEquations: scoreEquations,, *note solverMLE: solverMLE, computes the
solutions of this polynomial system and returns:

* the maximal value of the log-likelihood function attained by positive
definite matrices corresponding to such solutions,

* the positive definite matrices where the maximum is attained,

* the degree of the zero-dimensional ideal.

Be aware that this output might not correspond to the right MLE.



