solverMLE(...,ZeroTolerance=>...) -- optional input to set the largest absolute value that should be treated as zero
********************************************************************************************************************

  * Usage: 
        solverMLE(G,U,ZeroTolerance=>n)
  * Inputs:
      * n, a *note real number: (Macaulay2Doc)RR,, default is 1e-10

Description
===========

After computing the variety of the zero-dimensional ideal of the score
equations, solverMLE needs to determine which points lie in the PD cone. A
matrix is assumed to be positive definite if for all eigenvalues e:

-  *note realPart: (Macaulay2Doc)realPart, e > ZeroTolerance

-  *note abs: (Macaulay2Doc)abs, *note imaginaryPart:
(Macaulay2Doc)imaginaryPart, e <= ZeroTolerance

If an MLE matrix contains an imaginary part below the tolerance level, then
only the real part is reported in the output. (See  *note
checkPD(...,ZeroTolerance=>...):
checkPD_lp_pd_pd_pd_cmZeroTolerance=>_pd_pd_pd_rp,)





See also
========

  * *note checkPD: checkPD, -- returns positive definite matrices from a list
    of symmetric  matrices

